$DIR/main.p:25:2: cannot compile Bump[int] yet: T is an owner type parameter and int is not an owner
    The code of Bump ranges over a container of T and sees its elements as views
    of type *T, because T may be an owner. With int, which is not an owner, the
    container gives its elements by value, and this compiler does not yet keep
    the views in such an instance.
    Range over the indexes and take a pointer to each element, which works for
    both kinds of type:
        for i := range v.Len() {
            p := v.Ptr(i)
        }
    (see "No silent failures" in the Plutonium spec, section 21.2)
    (run "pluto explain E2500" for a longer explanation)
